3. Subtler mutation B — keep the suspectedContains check, remove ONLY
   deps.load(): FAILS with "did not refuse" (err == nil, write proceeds).
   This is the real vulnerability from the brief: without a fresh reload, both
   resolve.go's own check and the downstream loader check consult the SAME
   stale in-memory queue from the mint-time load, which still contains the
   key, so nothing catches the staleness. The test catches this half too.
All three mutations are caught; coverage is not limited to wholesale deletion.

